---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const example = `src/content/resources/
  my-water-shader/
    index.md        ← metadata (frontmatter) + documentation (Markdown)
    hero.webp       ← optional showcase image
    reference.webp  ← the effect under simple, honest conditions
    raw.webp        ← the input without the effect
    detail-1.webp   ← optional gallery images`;
---

<Base
  title="Contribute"
  description="How to suggest or add a resource to Open Tech Art: a Git-based workflow with one folder per resource."
  section="contribute"
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Contribute</p>
      <h1>Add a resource to the library</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The catalog lives in Git. Each resource is one folder holding a Markdown file and a few images, so
        adding one is a normal pull request. There are no forms and no accounts.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="cols">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Two ways to help</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <strong>Suggest a resource.</strong> <a href={SITE.issuesUrl}>Open an issue</a> with a link to the
            project and its license. That's enough for us to check it.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Add it yourself.</strong> Fork the repository, add a folder under
            <code>src/content/resources/</code>, run the build, and open a pull request.
          </li>
        </ol>

        <h2>What a resource looks like</h2>
        <pre><code>{example}</code></pre>
        <p>
          The folder name becomes the URL. The frontmatter is checked against a schema at build time, so
          mistakes show up as clear build errors rather than broken pages. Optional fields can be left out,
          and unknown compatibility should stay <code>unknown</code>.
        </p>

        <h2>Before you submit</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Link prominently to the original project, and credit the real creator.</li>
          <li>Confirm the resource is free <em>and</em> has an explicit open license. Record it accurately.</li>
          <li>Only include screenshots the license allows us to display. Keep them web-sized (WebP, ≤ 1920 px).</li>
          <li>Don't re-host the asset itself unless there's a strong reason and the license clearly allows it.</li>
          <li>Don't guess versions, pipelines or VR/mobile support.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Raw → Reference → Showcase</h2>
        <p>
          New entries should eventually include a <strong>Raw</strong> image (the input), a
          <strong>Reference</strong> image (the technique under simple conditions) and optionally a
          <strong>Showcase</strong> hero. Unusual techniques may need exceptions. Explain them in the entry,
          because honesty and clarity matter more than rigid rules.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="side">
        <div class="box">
          <h2>Full guidelines</h2>
          <p>The submission guidelines cover the schema fields, image rules and review checklist.</p>
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={SITE.newResourceUrl} rel="noopener">
            <Icon name="book" /> Submission guidelines
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="box">
          <h2>Repository</h2>
          <p>Development setup, build commands and deployment are documented in the README.</p>
          <a class="btn" href={SITE.repo} rel="noopener"><Icon name="github" /> View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding-top: 40px;
  }
  header {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.4vw, 2.7rem);
    margin: 8px 0 12px;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 300px;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .side {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--header-h) + 24px);
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .box {
    padding: 20px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--bg-raised);
  }
  .box h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .box p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0;
    }
    .side {
      position: static;
    }
  }
</style>
